{"kind":"request","text":"Implement P1f gate predicates and repeatable source-bound readiness tooling; independently publish the complete code while real protocol selection and operational gate success remain pending.","body":{"conditions":"Implement and independently publish phase A of the bounded P1f gate-and-selection package described in advisory report #1080 / 4015c4b1c700bb00ebf8937ff56eb020d9f296eb, accepted by root ratification #1081 / dabd5abb565ff46b9b09506f7ea31a0ad3b4e8a0. Read the full report before claiming. Start in a new isolated worktree from clean main 1c158d8044cd53ceed5cd191f1f423613c3c571e, preserving the existing protocol-closure and segmented-recovery evidence directories. This is the express implementation commission for executable gate predicates and readiness tooling, not a real protocol selection or permission for operational gate success. The original Marmot pair remains STOP. Preserve the selected Noseq ordering@1/recovery@2 semantics, D1-D9 choices and all current confidentiality/resource boundaries.\n\nDELIVERABLE AND ALLOWED SCOPE\nAdd a small gate wrapper/core, a development readiness runner and its strict evidence verifier. Proposed new paths are scripts/protocol-gate-core.ts, scripts/protocol-gate-readiness.ts, scripts/protocol-gate-readiness-evidence.ts, fixtures/crypto/gates/**, tests/protocol-gates/** and dedicated protocol-gates.config.ts / tsconfig.protocol-gates.json if needed. Focused edits may touch scripts/protocol-gates.ts, scripts/decision-types.ts, scripts/decision-validator.ts, scripts/decision-evidence.ts, scripts/decision-io.ts only for required trusted-input/persistence checks, package.json, docs/protocol-adoption.md and docs/toolchain.md. Only necessary evidence plumbing is allowed in scripts/protocol-closure.ts, scripts/protocol-closure-evidence.ts, scripts/decision-public-evidence.ts, fixtures/crypto/closure/profile.json, tests/protocol-closure/authority.test.ts and its fixture/challenge helpers. Publish an exhaustive exact final path map; these prospective paths do not excuse unrelated changes.\n\nNo new dependencies, crypto algorithms, provider/runtime pins, production services, Cloudflare/relay deployments, external signers, account/owner custody, P2-P9 code or larger resource limits. Do not edit README, notes or plans in this phase. The completed Atseq revision remains authoritative context; root coordinates the later narrow Plan/P2 wording reconciliation after actual selection. Preserve all historical failures and evidence without relabelling.\n\nCOMMANDS AND AUTHORITY\nImplement probe:protocol-gate-readiness and verify:protocol-gate-readiness as development commands that never open a real gate. Their exact source-bound E recursively verifies all 119 existing runtime cases, all ten existing authority groups with every one of their 71 required subchecks, plus a narrowly defined exhaustive new gate-case set. Keep the existing negative cases and the sorted/reversed unsigned-key positives. Distinguish runtime cases, authority groups and subchecks in evidence and prose.\n\nBoth public commands must support:\nnpm run test:crypto-feasibility -- --decision-export EXPORT --trust-policy POLICY --gitseq PINNED_BINARY --output NEW_DIRECTORY\nnpm run gate:protocol -- --decision-export EXPORT --trust-policy POLICY --gitseq PINNED_BINARY --output NEW_DIRECTORY\nThey verify the same previously selected immutable E and genuine signed authority on every invocation; they do not create a replacement E. E-only input, copied diagnostic results, synthetic policies, unknown/duplicate arguments and override/adopted/test switches refuse. Output directories must be fresh and evidence paths bounded. Success names bounded P1 G1-G5 passage for exact S/profile/E at F, D/AD/Q/P/R/AR and the operational commission; it makes no deployment or global-currentness claim and is not a bearer approval.\n\nReuse the actual pinned clean GitSeq d630 signature/chain audit and server-disabled local authority fold. Do not alter shared bin/gs, resident :8002, native strfry source/build or live-key custody. Trust policy is deliberately selected and controlled by the root/operator outside exports; accepting a filesystem path alone never establishes trust. The real public entry points enforce the actual Noseq genesis and independent real principal policy and refuse all generated-room policies. Pin exact source/base/tree, exhaustive artifact paths, profile/dependency/runtime/E/case/subcheck/decision expectations, minimum F, pinned verifier build/digest and operational commission ID. Generated-room positives remain in the separate development diagnostic API. Imported source objects stay data, never executable code. Check the loaded gate/checker module root and actual clean source S, runtime and dependencies; a valid bundle for S must not bless changed code currently executing elsewhere.\n\nVerify S/A/E -\u003e D -\u003e AD -\u003e Q -\u003e P -\u003e R -\u003e AR with explicit semantic order and all current effective-act, surviving-ratification, causal, independence, exact-guard/artifact/source/profile/raw-evidence, conflict and source-world checks. Selection D rests directly on every live selected A with a strict manifest; root AD follows D; Q follows AD and rests on D, AD and every A; R is the actual guarded strict decision-approval JSON at S; only Q's requester ratifies R. Publication-only review never substitutes.\n\nA later ordinary operational request C_op must be signed by the actual root, effective and unretired, have no_git_artifact=true, name the intended operator, exactly bind S/manifest/E and both allowed commands, and rest on the selected authority chain. F includes AR and C_op; trusted policy pins C_op. D/AD/R/AR alone cannot authorize real gate success. This implementation request is not C_op. The future operator will promise C_op, run both commands, retain V with commands/stdout/stderr/exits/source/policy/binary/export/result hashes and report it for root inspection. E must never contain V or future approval IDs.\n\nTRUSTED FRONTIER CUSTODY\nUse externally controlled nondecreasing minimum/high-water custody, with bounded atomic advancement and rejection of older/sibling frontiers. Claimed unverified depth cannot advance it. After verifying a complete signed descendant prefix, retain its high-water mark even if authority evaluation then discovers revocation and rejects the gate. A valid-old retry must not erase known revocation. Persistence failures must refuse success; document the supported local custody/atomicity assumptions and refusal/recovery behavior without claiming rollback-proof storage or P6 production crash atomicity. A first-contact hidden suffix or rolled-back trusted custody remains outside any global-currentness claim. Do not add a server or autonomous freshness service.\n\nACYCLIC PUBLICATION AND SELECTION\nAll executable gate/validator/evidence/test code is frozen before candidate C evidence and independent publication review. At C, real-room commands must still refuse because actual selection/operational authority is absent. Obtain all-path independent publication approval, requester-ratify it and perform guarded landing only after root reserves main. Root owns push and publication checkpoint. This implementation commitment completes at that reviewed landing.\n\nAfter publication, root will issue a separate ordinary evidence/selection-preparation request against exact landed S and its real live merge-successor artifacts. That work reruns the complete readiness package at S to produce final E; same tree/different commit cannot be relabelled. Only then may builder propose D, root ratify AD, and builder request actual independent decision review Q/P/R/AR. No second merge follows that decision-only review. The existing guard's decision-adoption mode is gs review --self-initiated D only when A is an actual already-published unassigned successor, not a reporting candidate or disguised assignment. Demonstrate this exact graph using generated signed fixtures before publication. If the actual later graph fails those predicates, stop and resolve it explicitly; do not waive source-world checks or invent a receipt alias. A later changed gate source needs fresh exact bindings.\n\nMake development evidence repeatable after selection: retain the real missing-selection negative against a named immutable pre-selection frontier F_pre, not the moving current room head. Introduce a readiness evidence version whose conclusion is observations checked, with no operational gate result. Do not erase the P1e historical decisions-unadopted observation or pretend it describes a later selected frontier. No future hash, approval ID, source-hash exclusion or new post-review patch is allowed.\n\nREQUIRED DISCRIMINATING CHECKS\nPreserve the full #997 coverage and add the bounded checks in #1080 section 4. Include actual public-CLI refusal of synthetic policy, copied result, absent/retired/non-root/wrong-scope commission and partial authority; actual generated signed publication -\u003e retired candidate/live successor -\u003e D/AD -\u003e fresh guarded decision review, with contaminated/direct-retired artifacts, later successor condemnation and publication-review reuse refusing; exact same-tree/different-commit evidence separation and different-tree refusal; changed loaded code, dirty source, runtime/verifier/profile/raw tampering, omitted new gate case or preserved subcheck, duplicate/failed/rehashed reports; fixed F_pre after later fixture adoption; nondecreasing trusted frontier including revocation failure followed by old valid input; persistence-error refusal; and all untouched later-stage commands still refusing. Reuse archived accepted E for isolated diagnostic positives to avoid self-reference, while enforcing real-public rejection. The real positive for final S occurs only later under genuine D/AD/Q/P/R/AR and C_op.\n\nRun actual fresh-cache-free npm ci/check/build, keep dedicated prepared typechecking mandatory, and run the full readiness command at clean candidate C. Preserve all prerequisite raw evidence and actual CLI outcomes; source-bound verification must reject every missing mandatory result. An independent reviewer must inspect every exact changed path and actually reproduce required execution/negative vectors. Read report #1080 for the G1-G5 mapping, D1-D9 residual exposures and later-stage distinctions; no additional crypto spike or production benchmark is authorized. Bound this package to two engineering days before an explicit complete/continue/change/stop report; surface material blockers early.\n\nFile fresh artifacts resting on this request/promise, then an explicit independent publication review request to noseq-reviewer. You alone requester-ratify that verdict and own guarded merge after root reservation. Preserve protected historical siblings and use ordinary staleness disclosure where appropriate; do not manufacture extra successor/retirement cleanup. Return the actual landed head/tree/receipt and retain all evidence. Stop there for root's next explicit evidence/selection request; do not adopt D1-D9 or run a real-success gate under this phase.","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","to":"981184b7467c74c2c8cd2783cb8bbc857427c7592a16425d0e2b7206a3768515"}}